{"name":"Sable Brown","hex":"#946a52","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sable","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small carnivorous mammal of the Old World that resembles a weasel, Martes zibellina, from cold regions in Eurasia and the North Pacific islands, valued for its dark brown fur.","Any other marten, especially Martes americana (syn. Mustela americana)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Sable-coloured, black.","In blazon, of the colour black."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sable"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sable","blocks":[{"text":"The sable is a species of marten, a small omnivorous mammal primarily inhabiting the forest environments of Russia, from the Ural Mountains throughout Siberia, and northern Mongolia. Its habitat also borders eastern Kazakhstan, China, North Korea, and Hokkaido, Japan."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Sobol_bur.jpg/330px-Sobol_bur.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sable"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown"},{"title":"Sable (tincture)","blocks":[{"text":"In heraldry, sable is the tincture equivalent to black. It is one of the five dark ti